WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.400
Face swaps replace or blend a face in an image or video.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.745
Lip-sync manipulation changes mouth movement to match different audio.

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:09.800
Voice cloning synthesizes speech that resembles a speaker.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.500
Each can be used with real footage, generated scenes, or edited recordings.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.300
AI-generated images can depict entirely fictional scenes or modify parts of real images.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.640
AI-generated video can create motion from prompts or animate still images.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.300
Quality varies,

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:27.200
and visible artifacts are becoming less dependable as generation systems improve.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.115
Synthetic documents and screenshots can imitate interfaces, messages, invoices, headlines,

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:33.085
or official forms.

00:00:33.085 --> 00:00:37.250
Their apparent structure may persuade viewers even when no underlying transaction, page,

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.200
or record exists.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:41.300
Verification should seek the original system or authoritative record.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:44.469
Staged media is real media arranged to create a false impression.

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:48.880
Miscontextualized media is genuine but presented with an incorrect date, place, identity,

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:50.000
or event description.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.395
These cases can be as harmful as generated content and may survive visual-deepfake checks.

00:00:54.395 --> 00:00:56.295
Hybrid manipulation combines methods.

00:00:56.295 --> 00:01:00.450
Real video may contain generated audio, edited timing, removed objects,

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.590
misleading captions, and synthetic frames.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.440
Labels should describe the supported finding rather than force every case into a single

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:07.095
category.

00:01:07.095 --> 00:01:09.290
Classifying the media is only part of the task.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:13.300
Analysts must evaluate the associated claim: who published it, what it asserts,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.470
how it spread, what independent records exist,

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:18.100
and what consequence follows if the claim is accepted.
